-- tremendously improved/addressed the issue of AI settlers staying parked for a very long time in cities when it should be safe enough or urgent enough to do so (in the early game as of now in our patch). For example Spain AI would have its first settler at turn +/- 45, and it would stay parked even at turn 100 in capital city, so it had only 1 city at turn 100!! Now after the change we get a settler later (random variation), but settle our 2nd city soon after around turn 60-70, and 3rd city around turn 80-90, so that we have 3 cities at turn 100 which is much nicer (settler production varies somehow, but we move much sooner after we have it now). They are also guarded enough it seems, and early we don't have that much threats, but a big priority to expand (quite safely but anyways etc). Changes made in `CvUnitAI::AI_found`. See [KI#68](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#68---tremendously-improved-ai-having-a-settler-parked-from-turn---45-to-turn-100-and-still-didnt-found-any-city-fixedaddressed-in-cvunitaiai_found) for details anyways etc.
