 - Reduce excessive civics change oscillation (was partially masked by civic_caste_system being almost always picked it seems based on autoplay testing, now more prevalent after our civic valuation changes that also value other civics depending on the player's strategic needs but anyways) by adding an additional percent slack new logic (and rewriting the old logic as well) in `CvPlayerAI::AI_doCivics` so that for example a new civic needs to be at least 10% higher valuated to be chosen/switched to (tunable). Note: If percent slack is set too high, it may cause AIs to switch too rarely and react more slowly, but if too low it may be inefficient especially for players that have anarchy turns on civic change—adjust to taste. Note 2: for some reason as of now in some cases bypassed by AIs entirely for some reason, to ideally investigate but for now if not always or not left as such anyways etc.
 - Fix the issue of civics that give specialist extra commerce (as of now civic_representation giving beakers, gold, culture) being almost never picked during the entire game (vs for example civic_heridetary_rule), even though the extra commerce per specialist should be quite attractive and strong especially if it applies to many specialists. Tweaked the commerce calculation formula in `CvPlayerAI::AI_civicValue` so it uses stronger advciv-sas's custom commerce weights, and stronger commerce multipliers derived from the SAS weights (both being tunable). Results in autoplay in much more prevalent as of now civic_representation picks especially in the mid/late game, with still some civic_heridetary_rule and civic_universal_suffrage picks and back and forth as well so hopefully balanced and should lead to stronger AI as the yields are overall stronger and economically more efficient generally but anyways etc.
 
