-- rebalanced or reworked some `DefaultUnitAI`, `UnitAIs`, and `NotUnitAIs` in the XML, to make AI go for most efficient roles, despite our units being more versatile now (see Military changes in [README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#military-and-some-civilian-units-related-info-non-exhaustive-see-sevopedia-orand-xml-for-details](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Custom_Main_Changes_Guide.md#military-and-some-civilian-units-related-info-non-exhaustive-see-sevopedia-orand-xml-for-details) for related info anyways etc). In short, even though as of now swordsmen can defend for all players as in for example having access to City Garrison promotions for example but anyways etc, they still, for AIs, will be used only and if not mostly as offensive units, as it is more efficient to do so in most cases, and the rare edge cases are not worth making AI weaker in most cases (like defending with swordsmen and attacking with longbowmen, which would cost more hammers for worse result generally anyways etc).
