-- Tremendously improved AI overbuilding very cheap (as of now 20 or less hammer cost in unitinfo XML (indepent from any trainpercent modifier if i am not mistaken anyways etc)) combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now anyways etc) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient, nonsensical since there are so many better options like swordsmen, chariots, longbowmen, anything else basically some of which not requiring any bonus if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc, and easy to overshoot if i may say but anyways etc, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units anyways etc, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless. Since they are easy to overbuild due to being so cheap, they may quickly make us bankrupt, and are not so effective per unit. As in our mod archers are as of now available very soon, fairly cheap, and more versatile and overall stronger, plus since they also help fill our defense needs/quotas sooner so we move to offense focus sooner, it seems very nice to be able to cut down on excess very cheap units, as of now only the ancient maceman (note: this trims down scouts as well since they have combat if i am not mistaken, but we don't seem to overproduce them so fine anyways etc, and even if we were to then would be handled by the same cap if i am not mistaken but anyways etc). As a result of these changes in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, ingame, we seem to have much better compositions (e.g. 3 ancient macemen at turn 100-130 vs 11 before in AI players), and much more stronger units in comparison. Hopefully helps being economically efficient as well. AI should be stronger as a result of these changes hopefully if i am not mistaken but anyways etc. See for details [53.4 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding very cheap combat units (ancient macemen only being an issue as of now anyways etc) in the early game, sometimes even at turn 100, which is inefficient and easy to overshoot if i may say but anyways etc, as they are cheap and accumulate quickly, but are not too effective especially as soon as we get archer units anyways etc, now limited, especially even more so after as of now turn 50 where they should be especially useless; much better military compositions and better growth as a result anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#534-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-very-cheap-combat-units-ancient-macemen-only-being-an-issue-as-of-now-anyways-etc-in-the-early-game-sometimes-even-at-turn-100-which-is-inefficient-and-easy-to-overshoot-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-as-they-are-cheap-and-accumulate-quickly-but-are-not-too-effective-especially-as-soon-as-we-get-archer-units-anyways-etc-now-limited-especially-even-more-so-after-as-of-now-turn-50-where-they-should-be-especially-useless-much-better-military-compositions-and-better-growth-as-a-result-anyways-etc) anyways etc. Update: now the anti excess very cheap units is also included in `CvCity::doTurn` in the no production fallback unit code, as we were producing too many fallback ancient macemen otherwise with the new offense only code (like 19 ancient macemen at turn 100 which is very inefficient and most likely to bankrupt us or ruin our game but anyways etc) anyways etc. Update 2: Also added renaissance plus (anti pikemen or such, but only for land AND direct combat units (no scouts, spies, etc.)) logic as well as these units are ineffective against gun and higher units, and economically very inefficient (high spam and unit cost, low combat potential vs lower unit costs for stronger units or/and possibly more buildings as well i mean but anyways etc).
